# Force git to treat these as pure binary — never touch their bytes.
# Without this, Windows git (core.autocrlf=true, which is the default on
# Windows) silently rewrites LF <-> CRLF inside every tracked file it
# thinks is text. A PyTorch .pt checkpoint is a zip archive full of raw
# bytes, so that "conversion" mangles it — which is exactly what produces
# "file is empty, truncated or corrupted (EOFError: Ran out of input)"
# the moment Render's clone tries to torch.load() it, even though the
# file looks fine on your own machine.
*.pt binary
*.pth binary
*.onnx binary
*.db binary
*.sqlite binary
*.sqlite3 binary
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
